From 4bfe1259e80ccee6abe9dbf9adf82d32872c73ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: belikh <io@jupiter.au>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 10:00:49 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] redox-rt, generic-rt: add mips64 n32 (SGI Indy)

redox-rt/src/arch/mips64.rs: SigArea and ArchIntRegs ($1..$31, pc, hi, lo
as u64), the fork wrapper and fork return (callee-saved s0..s7, gp, fp, ra;
soft float, no FPU state), thread start, current_sp, deactivate_tcb,
arch_pre/arch_ret_to_sig. The signal trampoline is a trap until it is
written. STACK_TOP is 0x8000_0000 minus the kernel metadata pages.

Thread pointer convention: $gp ($28) holds &tcb_ptr + 8, so the TCB pointer
is read at -8($28). Static code with no GOT leaves $gp free.

Signed-off-by: belikh <io@jupiter.au>
Signed-off-by: belikh <io@belic.net>
